  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Show that for $y=x^2+2mx+m^2+n^2$, the graph is always touching or above the $x$-axis for all real values of $m$ and $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\Delta=-4n^2\\leq0$ and $a=1>0$. The graph touches the $x$-axis when $n=0$ and lies entirely above it when $n\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(2m)^2-4(1)(m^2+n^2)\\\\\\Delta&=4m^2-4m^2-4n^2\\\\\\Delta&=-4n^2\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n^2\\geq0$, $\\Delta\\leq0$. Also, $a=1>0$, so the parabola is concave up. When $n=0$, $\\Delta=0$ and the graph touches the $x$-axis. When $n\\ne0$, $\\Delta<0$ and the graph lies entirely above the $x$-axis.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
